{
  "$comment": [
    "Canonical book-name mapping across the project's three independent book vocabularies.",
    "Written because the same book is named differently in each, and three separate",
    "cross-workstream errors were caused by comparing them as strings: a graph/MASTER",
    "overlap reported as 0 when it is 5, plus two earlier naming mismatches.",
    "",
    "COMPARE ON canonical_id, NEVER on a display name.",
    "",
    "  graph_book   = (:Book).name in Neo4j, seeded from db_exports (June snapshot)",
    "  master_book  = the `book` field in data/corpus/MASTER_corpus.jsonl",
    "  page_store   = directory under data/vision_pass/pages/",
    "  title        = MASTER `book_title`, which is what actually proves the identity",
    "",
    "Membership is genuinely uneven, and that is the point of the table:",
    "  - 5 books are in BOTH the graph and MASTER (the Phase-1 set)",
    "  - Tirthaji is in the graph and the page store but NOT merged into MASTER",
    "  - 20 exam-pillar books are in MASTER and the page store but NOT in the graph",
    "",
    "There is still NO question-level join between the graph and MASTER (id overlap is",
    "0), so this table maps books, not questions. A page-level mapping for the shared 5",
    "is the tractable next step; the corpus->graph question mapping remains unbuilt and",
    "gates any extraction output reaching the runtime."
  ],
